t(43, 385, """Whoever is afflicted with sins and disobedience and conceals it is better than one afflicted with them who then "stands on a pulpit" advising people! The first is a disobedient sinner between himself and his Lord; the second is a hypocrite, recorded as a hypocrite, and it is feared he will die a hypocrite! Do not advise anything unless you have first set it right in yourself and applied it, before advising people with it.""")

t(43, 795, """The challenges that moral responsibilities impose on our lives are neither a stroll nor a joke. Those strolling and joking today are 90% of mankind! The rest are between those lost from the road and those walking on it! The truth is that neither the Prophet ﷺ, nor his household, nor his Companions praised in the Book of our Great Lord lived only praying, fasting, giving zakat and performing umrah! How easy this Islam would be! Rather they lived on earth as Qur'an, guidance and light, stars moving upon the earth. For those people after the Prophet ﷺ saw that the earth never ceases to need unending reform; they realised they were not created in vain, and realised it did not befit them to say what they do not do. So they reformed the earth with the reform of the righteous, not the reform of the hypocrite who says what he does not do; his reform amounts to nothing, rather through him the earth is corrupted more and more.""")

t(43, 1460, """There is in history no great message carried, no rugged road crossed, no decisive steps walked, no great hardships overcome, no heavy challenges faced, without a great price. Whoever thinks the cost is bearable and the price within reach of every spirit, every soul and every will is not on that road, nor even close to it! None will hold out to the end except one who grasps that destinies are not tailored to the measure of the wayfarer and the walker, but tailored to the measure of the message whose carrying was decreed as destiny. Man was charged with it as a chosen responsibility, loaded with it as a duty not an honour, tested by it as trial and examination; it was written upon him to add to his loads, not lift them; to magnify his pains, not ease them; to bloody his feet, not bandage them! To carry the message or to betray it: this is the hardest question in man's life, from Adam, peace be upon him, until the death of the last believing soul on this earth.""")

t(43, 2140, """Praise be to Allah for the safe return! Man has gone back to using his mouth to speak, not his hand! After 20 years of using his hand to speak instead of his mouth! In the greatest historic operation of contempt for the sons and daughters of Adam in the name of technology, the greatest organised operation of social destruction, unprecedented in the history of the sons and daughters of Adam on earth, and the greatest historically unprecedented wrecking of man's innate abilities for sound, successful communication between him and the sons and daughters of his kind!""")

t(44, 1315, """{Say: Are those who know equal to those who do not know?} .. And everyone on earth has his role for which Allah the Exalted created him""")

t(45, 175, """After the great war, Allah the Exalted willing, electricity will exist and will continue, by the permission of Allah the Exalted, for years""")

t(45, 1605, """Nothing in a person's life is greater than housing fit for a human being; everything after that is of lower rank to him""")

t(46, 580, """Even surplus modern shopping centres offer good housing solutions for residents""")

t(46, 2030, """The absurd question the West has exported to the world since the eighteenth century, specifically since 1792, and concentrated intensely on exporting since the nineteenth century, about equality between man and woman, was a question expressing an internal crisis within the West itself, since the West for a very long time (thousands of years) did not know what to do with the woman in its midst or how to classify her within its social system. Whereas for a thousand and nearly 500 years the woman in the Islamic world has been classified, with clearly defined rights and duties, her human identity not unknown in the lands of this Islamic world. The crisis was always in the West, not with us. And when the West woke up one morning to decide to set a definition for woman .. to decide that she is a human being .. and when it set its own definitions of woman .. and approved its own classification of her .. it decided to teach us how to define woman and how to classify her, when we are the ones who protected her in our region from Marrakesh to Jakarta for 1447 years; she herself knew what she was, and always knew what she wanted within this Islamic world, while the West was late in giving her her rights all that time!""")

t(47, 55, """No person can accept the idea that a novice pupil, who entered a human school 300 years ago, where he learned that woman is a human being only 300 years ago, should try to present himself as a teacher to an Ummah that entered a divine school 1450 years ago?! We are the master and we are the teacher.

The West does not look at the world with the eye of logic; its view has always been one of strength and weakness .. And those who admire it, its classifications and its desire to impose its opinion on the whole world would do well to read this post.""")

t(47, 625, """When admitting a mistake is costly, the truth disappears and is buried deep, and the system of any work begins to collapse .. a hospital .. a school.. a company .. a shop .. and so on .. also a family .. social relations .. everything .. Because truth alone is what protects the cohesion of any system and provides it with the moral context that is always a lever for it to continue strong, not merely to continue!""")

t(47, 2470, """Hadith: "You will make a secure peace with the Romans" .. to the end of the hadith""")

t(48, 1345, """Chancellor of Germany: 40 thousand visas are granted yearly to Indian experts from the Indian city of Bangalore

This is how states are run, by attracting experts and expertise

The city of Bangalore is the home of software technology and artificial intelligence in India""")

t(48, 1875, """One of the followers asked about this hadith: "A time will surely come upon people when a man goes around with charity of gold and then finds no one to take it from him, and one man will be seen followed by forty women seeking refuge with him, because of the scarcity of men and the abundance of women."
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: Sahih

This can only be understood, and Allah our Great Lord knows best, as being after the Great Battle (al-Malhamah al-Kubra), not before it. After the Great Battle the model of the modern world economy falls because of the fall of Europe after that great war, and the modern system of man's present life that we live today collapses, and the needs of the Muslims are completely fulfilled, with no poverty and no lack. Every Muslim has his house, his farmland, his water well, his crops, his livestock and his poultry, and people no longer even need markets, buying or selling. So what people have known for thousands of years collapses: man's need of man, man's need of the state, and man's need of trade, internal and external. This coincides in time with the small number of men compared to the number of women because of the Great Battle that takes place in northern Syria. So charity is carried around and no one takes it, because it is not permissible for anyone to take it, otherwise he sins! This is the time of the scooping out of wealth, which I explained in an earlier post a short while ago.""")

t(49, 350, """Our Great Lord created His servants because He loved them and does not need them. Servants made things to use them because they loved themselves and needed the things. Our Great Lord created us to enjoy what He created for us and to worship Him, and worship is thanks for the blessings and for His having, hallowed be His names, brought us into being. This is called love. We make things not out of love for them but out of love for ourselves, because we make them so that we benefit from them, not so that they benefit from us. As for our Great Lord, He created us so that we benefit from Him, Mighty and Exalted far above all; it is not He, hallowed be His names and attributes, who benefits from us.

The question then: in what does Allah the Exalted benefit from us? The answer: He benefits from us in nothing.
The angels worship Him, the birds worship Him, inanimate things worship Him, the trees worship Him, and all the kingdoms of creatures other than man worship Him, those we know of and those we do not; among the jinn are believers who worship Him, hallowed be His names. Man came after the creation of the jinn, and before us the believers among the jinn performed the acts of worship. So our Great Lord did not create us because we are the only ones in His dominion.

So He created us because He loves us .. and worship is thanks for this love .. and to Allah belongs the highest example .. When people love one another they exchange gifts! But those of mankind who have gone astray find no need to say thank You to Allah the Exalted! A strange thing! They thank one another for the favours done among them! Yet they do not remember that merely being created on earth was a great blessing upon them, that they came into this life, and that their Lord created them and gave them the enjoyment of mother, father, wife, offspring, food, drink and thousands of things!

He created us, hallowed be His names and attributes, because He loves us .. The hardships of life are affliction and trial: affliction for the disobedient, and if he returns and repents he lives a pleasant life; or a trial for the believer, and the believer in trial laughs! So to those who say He created us because He loves us and then put difficulties in life, I say firmly: you are not being tried; rather affliction has come down on you because you do not worship Him. Otherwise the one being tried who worships Him as He deserves does not grumble. As soon as you hear someone grumbling about life's hardships, know that he does not worship Allah as He deserves, and Allah the Exalted is punishing him because he does not want to say thank You to Allah the Exalted. And this thank You is obligatory and required. Otherwise everyone who says it is not required is playing games, and this game-playing "does not work on me or on people"; he is playing games because when a servant like himself offers him something he thanks him. Since you thanked a servant like yourself, do not tell me I do not necessarily have to offer thanks to Allah.

He created us, hallowed be His names and attributes, because He loves us .. So whoever of His servants is tried with something was a believer, and Allah and people found him patient and steadfast .. And whoever is struck by the affliction of punishment is a non-believer who denies the duty of thanks, like the runaway slave who has fled his master, wandering aimlessly from city to city, his clothes ragged, his feet filthy, and people do not look at him with respect. So know, O every runaway who refuses to thank Allah the Great and refuses to worship Him, that in this state no one respects you, because you were created out of love and you denied the love of Allah the Exalted for you, and threw back the favour of Allah the Exalted upon you with ingratitude and denial. Therefore Allah the Exalted detested you, and you went astray on earth, wandering aimlessly!""")

t(49, 2190, """Will the Mahdi scoop out wealth by handfuls, or scoop out gold by handfuls?! And will he scoop out wealth from the first day? And will the scooping of wealth happen because of the mountain of gold?

A question that reached me .. Before answering it, another wording in the hadith of overflowing wealth must be understood. As for the two wordings, the first is "he gives wealth sihahan" (meaning evenly, that is, equally among people), and in Ahmad the wording is "he gives wealth sihahan ((until)) he orders a caller who calls out: Whoever has a need of me..." to the end of the hadith, which is long.

The word (((until))) in the hadith: this word is an important word .. because it indicates passing from one stage to""")

t(50, 60, """a stage .. You say: I walked a distance of a kilometre until I reached the shop. Clearly there is a lapse of time in it, and clearly there is a passing from one stage to another .. What I understand, and Allah the Exalted knows best, in the matter of scooping out wealth and the difference between scooping it and giving wealth evenly is something for which I find many rational proofs in understanding and comprehension. Explaining the question of the distribution of wealth in the time of the Mahdi is important, because the hadiths contain two wordings that do not agree, and each is a wording with a sound chain. They are the wording (sihahan), meaning distributing wealth with justice and fairness among people, and the wording (scooping out wealth). At the same time the two do not agree in meaning, because distributing wealth equally is the opposite of scooping it in terms of the act itself. I divide 20 dinars between two people, meaning I give each of them 10 dinars. But if I scoop out wealth to them, it means the first will take an unknown number of dinars and the second will take an unknown number of dinars; so how would I have divided the wealth between them evenly, that is, equally, as in the wording (sihahan)? This difficulty was noticed by very few of the commentators to begin with, and among the mujtahids I found none who dealt with it by explanation, although it is important for people to know what is coming in their lives, for those who will witness that time!

What my understanding has settled on is two points:
The first: wealth is distributed equally and fairly according to people's needs and ages. This is a first stage in the life of the Ummah in that era, meaning there is no scooping of wealth, only equal distribution. Most likely, as I understand it, the reason is that the Ummah needs thousands of things lacking in people's lives, and this requires a budget and civil, industrial, agricultural, food, construction and military spending, and more, given people's needs for houses, streets, infrastructure and thousands of other needs!

The second: wealth is scooped out by handfuls. The scooping of wealth means the state has completed all its responsibilities towards the people, built the houses, cities and streets, and founded productive cities, not consumer cities; the difference between the two is like that between sky and earth. Even so its public spending continued, and it employed non-Muslims in 95% of non-military public jobs, because wealth is not scooped out for them; the scooping is for Muslims only. The world economy collapsed after the Great Battle, the system of international cooperation collapsed, Europe fell as is known from the hadith of the Great Battle, the world changed, and the Muslims no longer lack houses, streets, markets, plants, livestock or anything.

Summary: the future of the Ummah for that generation .. Justice in distributing wealth, which means everyone lives an equal life with all his needs in life met, so that the excuses for not worshipping Allah the Exalted fall away from him. Then wealth is scooped out because it will overflow.

So they are two dissimilar stages. Two stages different politically, economically and humanly.

The stage of the Ummah's glory that the Prophet ﷺ described as lasting up to 7 or 8 or 9 years, and it will be in Bayt al-Maqdis as in the wording of the hadith (the difference in the number of years, according to some scholars, is due to the narrators' doubt and is not from the words of the Prophet ﷺ). The Prophet ﷺ described those 9 years as years of glory for the Ummah, and he ﷺ said: ((and the Ummah becomes great)) .. This is the stage of distributing wealth equally, not the stage of scooping out wealth; wealth is distributed to the Muslims equally.

Finally, many think the cause of wealth in that era and that age is the mountain of gold alone! The truth is that this is short-sighted thinking. Wealth is scooped out not because of the mountain of gold; rather I understand the mountain of gold as a lever for the economy, such that minting a world currency the world demands becomes possible only in the hands of the Muslims, because they possess gold backing a strong currency, as was the case at the start of the era when the world agreed on the dollar after the Second World War, before the Americans severed the link between gold backing and the value of the dollar. Clearly the world has been used, since the Second World War, to agreeing on a world currency that gives the world back the spirit of the economy. So the wealth of the Ummah will not be caused by the mountain of gold alone; rather the Ummah's coming economic cycle is a state that will bring into the Ummah many great funds and investments, which will make wealth pile up and multiply in it, from sources other than the mountain of gold known in the famous hadith.

As for the stage of scooping out wealth, it is the stage in which this world order ends and collapses, so that distributing gold becomes possible. This, and Allah knows best, happens after the Great Battle in which Europe collapses entirely and comprehensively, and with that Great Battle the whole world's economy collapses, and the whole world enters the stage of the end of manufacturing and the end of world peace, and the sign of the Smoke and the appearance of the Dajjal draw near. So gold is distributed to the people in full, and the Muslims are owners of farms and houses, their food in their hands, with cities producing crops and animal food, their life having moved to another, new and different dimension. Here the scooping of wealth (gold) becomes understandable and its cause clear!""")

t(51, 250, """The destroyer of the Arab person's health in the twentieth and twenty-first centuries""")

t(51, 1740, """The worst thing that happens to a person every morning is: the journey to work every day in this way that destroys the nerves, ruins the mood, shatters inner security and makes a person lose his soul because he turns into a production machine! Whereas the residents of small model cities productive in industry or agriculture and livestock do not live this nonsense!""")

t(52, 810, """Mansa Musa (king of Mali) distributed huge quantities of gold in Cairo during his journey on his way to Hajj, which led to the collapse of the value of gold in Egypt and a crazy rise in prices for years! So is the coming age the age of the return of gold and silver? The answer is yes, but not under an economy that matches today's economy!

The question many people raise is: what if there were so much gold in the world that people could buy at any time and buy everything they need?

To simplify the picture: if a great deal of gold suddenly appeared covering everyone's needs, we would face one of two scenarios, and both make gold lose its basic feature as "currency":

1. Loss of "scarcity value" (runaway inflation)
The secret of gold's power lies in its being rare. If we found "mountains" of gold that let everyone own it in abundance, a simple economic phenomenon would occur: "The more supply rises, the less the value."
The merchant will ask you for 10 kilograms of gold for one loaf of bread, because gold is plentiful in everyone's hands.
This happened historically with Mansa Musa (king of Mali) when he distributed huge quantities of gold in Cairo during his journey to Hajj, which led to the collapse of gold's value and a crazy rise in prices for years.
2. Gold turning into "metal paper"
If gold were plentiful and available like aluminium or iron, it would lose its function as a store of value. Central banks and people love gold because it cannot be printed or found easily.
If it became abundant, it would behave exactly like today's paper currencies (inflation, loss of value, fluctuation), but with an added flaw: it is heavy and hard to transport.
The historical paradox (stability of quantity is the secret)
Gold succeeded as currency for thousands of years not because it was enough for everyone, but because its quantity grew very slowly through mining, which kept a relative balance with the growth of mankind at the time.
Imagine this situation:
If someone told you that "sand" is the new currency, would you work and toil to obtain it when it lies in abundance on the beaches? Of course not. "Too much" gold would make its value like sand; no one would agree to sell you his effort or his goods for a metal that anyone can easily obtain and that is available in everyone's hands.
Summary: the power of money is not in its "quantity" but in its "purchasing power", which results from its rarity and the difficulty of obtaining it.


So why do many economists today call for the return of gold as currency?
The secret lies in that these economists (most of them from the Austrian school) do not look at gold as a daily "means of payment" but as a "moral and political restraint" on governments.
Here are the reasons that make them demand a return to gold despite all the obstacles:""")

t(53, 55, """1. Stopping the "printing press" (preventing inflation)
In the current system governments can print trillions of dollars at the press of a button, which reduces the purchasing power of your savings (it is a kind of hidden tax). In the gold system, the government cannot print money unless it extracts real gold, and this forces it into financial discipline and not living beyond its means.
2. Preserving the value of "people's toil"
The advocates of gold see paper currencies as a "deception". If you saved 1000 dollars today, in 10 years it may buy you half of what it buys now. Gold, however, has kept its purchasing power for thousands of years.
Returning to gold means the value of your effort does not evaporate over time through political decisions.
3. Stability of international trade
At present strong currencies (like the dollar) dominate the world, and any shock in America's economy affects everyone.
Gold is a neutral "world language" not controlled by any single state. Returning to it means stable exchange rates and preventing "currency wars".
4. Curbing runaway debt
The current system rests on endless debt because money is "cheap" and easy to print. The gold system makes borrowing hard and costly, which prevents "economic bubbles" like the one that caused the 2008 crisis.
How do they propose the return? (Not with coins in the pocket)
Most of these economists do not propose that you carry gold in your wallet; they propose a "digital gold system":
You use your bank card or your phone as normal.
But every digital "riyal" or "dollar" issued by the bank must have a set weight of gold stored in the treasury.
In this way we combine the ease of technology and the safety of gold.
In short: they call for gold as an "anchor" for the ship so that the waves of inflation and debt do not toss it about, not as the ship's only "sail".

The view of most contemporary Muslim economists (such as Dr. Monzer Kahf and Dr. Rafiq al-Masri) meets that of the supporters of the "gold system" in the West, but from a Shariah and moral starting point that sees the current monetary system as containing a structural flaw.
Their vision is summed up in the following points:
1. Gold and silver are the "origin" in monetary legislation
Many hold that Islam tied major Shariah rulings (such as zakat, blood money and the punishment for theft) to set amounts of gold and silver. This tie gave the two metals a special standing as "the just measure of values", which pushes towards the necessity of returning to them or to a stable currency that imitates their stability, to protect people's rights.
2. The prohibition of "loss of purchasing power" (financial injustice)
Muslim economists view the inflation that results from printing paper currency as a kind of "consuming people's wealth unjustly". When the currency loses its value, savers and the poor are harmed most. Therefore the return to gold is considered a means of achieving the justice and equality that the Shariah objective stipulates.
3. Combating riba
The current paper system is tightly bound to the system of interest (riba); money is created through "debts". In the gold system, money is a substance with value in itself and cannot be created from nothing. These economists hold that returning to gold would reduce the dominance of the interest-based economy and direct investments towards the real economy (trade and production).
4. Sovereignty of the Islamic Ummah
There is a current calling for the "Islamic gold dinar" (like the calls of Dr. Mahathir Mohamad) as a means of breaking dependence on the US dollar, which grants Islamic states real economic independence that protects their wealth from external political fluctuations.
Even so.. there is a "realist" current among scholars of Islamic economics:
This current (like the opinions of the International Islamic Fiqh Academy) holds that:
Current paper currencies are Shariah "prices" (athman), and the rulings that apply to gold and silver (such as riba and zakat) apply to them.
A physical return to gold is very hard under the present balance of world powers, so they focus on "strengthening the currency" through production and justice instead of merely changing its material.
Summary: Muslim economists agree that gold is "the most just scale", but they divide between "revolutionaries" who demand an immediate return to the metal, and **"reformers"** who demand that the current paper currency be regulated""")

t(54, 60, """by gold standards or a basket of commodities to achieve justice.

The government of the Malaysian state of Kelantan in 2010 minted real gold dinars and silver dirhams. The aim was for people to use them in their daily life instead of the paper "ringgit" (Malaysia's official currency).
2. How did they integrate gold and silver into trade?
Setting the value: the dinar (gold) was issued for large transactions and savings, and the dirham (silver) for small purchases (such as bread or meals).
The merchants' network: thousands of merchants and restaurants joined the initiative, and they put stickers on their shops saying: "We accept payment in dinar and dirham".
Salaries and zakat: the state began paying part of employees' salaries (optionally) in coins, and encouraged people to pay zakat in gold and silver to revive the Prophetic Sunnah in this matter.
3. The difficulties they faced (why did it not become the basic currency?)
Law and sovereignty: Malaysia's central bank considered these coins "commemorative pieces" and not official legal tender (Legal Tender), which prevented imposing them as a full alternative to paper.
Price fluctuation: people found it hard to know the daily price; the restaurant had to change the price of a meal in dirhams daily based on the world silver price, which is exhausting for consumer and merchant.
Hoarding: instead of spending the gold, people bought it and stored it (hoarding) because they knew its value rises, and went on spending paper because it loses its value.
4. The shift to "digital gold"
After this experiment the Malaysians realised that carrying metal in the pocket is hard, so they set up platforms such as HelloGold (the first Shariah-compliant gold platform), which lets people buy gold and silver through a mobile app and use them as savings or a digital means of payment.
Summary of Malaysia's experiment: integration is possible "morally" and at the popular level, but it faces huge legal and political obstacles, because states do not easily give up their right to print paper currency.""")

t(55, 145, """In car factories in the last century the engineer had the final word and the accountant obeyed the engineer's order, so cars were of strong steel, steady on the ground, protecting the driver and passengers better .. Then the accountant came in the twenty-first century and said to the engineer: your role is over .. step back .. Then the final word became the accountant's .. Cars of paper for the sake of a lower production cost .. and less safety and security for driver and passengers .. What matters is that the factory profits .. The factory bears a lower production cost and sells at a higher price than twentieth-century prices .. In the coming age, Allah the Exalted willing, authority must be returned to the engineer and the accountant sent to his office to do the accounting work the engineer orders him to do, not the reverse! Note: this post is not against accountants .. This post is only an expression of the defect that has struck the way car factories are run, and in the end the accountant was given the decisive word in the car industry in our time by order of the owner .. The fault is not originally the accountant's.""")

t(55, 2045, """When they distorted their book they wrote in it about your city: "You will be demolished and never be built again, forever!" They lied, by Allah's permission, for our promise is truth from our Great Lord, and their promise to themselves is false, because their hands wrote it and their minds composed it!""")

t(56, 1010, """In 2024, 2025, 2026 and perhaps 2027 this shore was completely demolished, and in 2027 or 2028, and Allah knows best, it will have been completely built""")

